    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a thyroid storm, and we'll know more once the an ECG is back.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:27",
      "end_timestamp": "04:37",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Let's get an ECG, for fast heart rhythm. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'll start you on propranolol, 1 milligrams, now, single dose. That's for thyroid storm. This is an emergency, you will be treated in high dependency. Let's get you seen by the emergency team, I'll arrange the letter. See me again straight away.",
